{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1569,
    "dDurationMs": 4431,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Physicists tell us that the universe is expanding,\nbut does that mean we expand with it?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6000,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, if so, wouldn't no one notice because\neverything would scale up at the same relative"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9660,
    "dDurationMs": 2189,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "size and it would seem like nothing had changed?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11849,
    "dDurationMs": 2931,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, the truth is, the universe isn't expanding."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14780,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Space is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15780,
    "dDurationMs": 3850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of course, everything else in the universe\nis \"in\" space, and ignoring the influence"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19630,
    "dDurationMs": 4139,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of any other forces, when the space between\nthings expands, those things will appear to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23769,
    "dDurationMs": 1541,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be carried farther apart."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25310,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there are other forces in the universe,\nand their strengths aren't directly affected"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28820,
    "dDurationMs": 1049,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when space expands."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29869,
    "dDurationMs": 4341,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, gravity and electromagnetism\nare able to hold atoms and solar systems together"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34210,
    "dDurationMs": 4550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because these forces are too strong for the\nslow expansion of space to overcome."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38760,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Think of it like this - if you and your cat\nare standing on a piece of ground that starts"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42800,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to stretch horizontally between you, the ground\nwill pull you and your cat away from each"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46840,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47840,
    "dDurationMs": 3449,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if the leash is strong enough - in particular,\nif it's stronger than the friction force between"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51289,
    "dDurationMs": 4270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your feet and the ground - it'll hold you\nand your cat together as space expands beneath"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55559,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56559,
    "dDurationMs": 2570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the real universe, it's the strength of\nthe electromagnetic force that determines"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59129,
    "dDurationMs": 4110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the effective sizes of particles, atoms, and\nmolecules so that even if the space they're"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63239,
    "dDurationMs": 3211,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in expands, the molecules don't."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66450,
    "dDurationMs": 3940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Electromagnetism is basically the leash that\nholds atoms and molecules together - and gravity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70390,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is the leash that holds solar systems and\ngalaxies together."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73330,
    "dDurationMs": 4679,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Only over super super long distances is gravity's\nattraction weak enough and the cumulative"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78009,
    "dDurationMs": 4430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "expansion of all that space big enough to\ncause galaxies and galactic clusters to actually"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82439,
    "dDurationMs": 4401,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "grow more distant from one another over time\n- we know this because the light from distant"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86840,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "galaxies gets red-shifted as it's stretched\nby the expansion of the space it's traveling"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90860,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91860,
    "dDurationMs": 4420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Gravity certainly still pulls distant objects\ntowards each other, but space expands faster."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96280,
    "dDurationMs": 12260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Basically, the cat is "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108540,
    "dDurationMs": 23190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "off "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131730,
    "dDurationMs": 4570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the leash."
    } ]
  } ]
}
